{"audio": "1corinthians-09.opus", "duration_ms": 233774, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 5160, "text": "1 Corinthians, Chapter Nine."}, {"start_ms": 5160, "end_ms": 6060, "text": "Am I not free?"}, {"start_ms": 6700, "end_ms": 8000, "text": "Am I not an apostle?"}, {"start_ms": 8481, "end_ms": 10681, "text": "Have I not seen Jesus our Lord?"}, {"start_ms": 11421, "end_ms": 14141, "text": "Are you yourselves not my workmanship in the Lord?"}, {"start_ms": 14821, "end_ms": 18821, "text": "Even if I am not an apostle to others, surely I am to you."}, {"start_ms": 19341, "end_ms": 22121, "text": "For you are the seal of my apostleship in the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 23041, "end_ms": 28682, "text": "This is my defense to those who scrutinize me: Have we no right to food and to drink?"}, {"start_ms": 29102, "end_ms": 35082, "text": "Have we no right to take along a believing wife, as do the other apostles and the Lord’s brothers and Cephas?"}, {"start_ms": 35802, "end_ms": 39682, "text": "Or are Barnabas and I the only apostles who must work for a living?"}, {"start_ms": 40702, "end_ms": 43483, "text": "Who serves as a soldier at his own expense?"}, {"start_ms": 43883, "end_ms": 46683, "text": "Who plants a vineyard and does not eat of its fruit?"}, {"start_ms": 47303, "end_ms": 49903, "text": "Who tends a flock and does not drink of its milk?"}, {"start_ms": 50643, "end_ms": 52863, "text": "Do I say this from a human perspective?"}, {"start_ms": 53463, "end_ms": 55203, "text": "Doesn’t the Law say the same thing?"}, {"start_ms": 55743, "end_ms": 64544, "text": "For it is written in the Law of Moses: “Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain.” Is it about oxen that God is concerned?"}, {"start_ms": 65244, "end_ms": 67644, "text": "Isn’t He actually speaking on our behalf?"}, {"start_ms": 68444, "end_ms": 76825, "text": "Indeed, this was written for us, because when the plowman plows and the thresher threshes, they should also expect to share in the harvest."}, {"start_ms": 77565, "end_ms": 83485, "text": "If we have sown spiritual seed among you, is it too much for us to reap a material harvest from you?"}, {"start_ms": 84385, "end_ms": 88565, "text": "If others have this right to your support, shouldn’t we have it all the more?"}, {"start_ms": 89345, "end_ms": 91625, "text": "But we did not exercise this right."}, {"start_ms": 92026, "end_ms": 96226, "text": "Instead, we put up with anything rather than hinder the gospel of Christ."}, {"start_ms": 97226, "end_ms": 104486, "text": "Do you not know that those who work in the temple eat of its food, and those who serve at the altar partake of its offerings?"}, {"start_ms": 105166, "end_ms": 111447, "text": "In the same way, the Lord has prescribed that those who preach the gospel should receive their living from the gospel."}, {"start_ms": 112167, "end_ms": 114587, "text": "But I have not used any of these rights."}, {"start_ms": 115127, "end_ms": 118987, "text": "And I am not writing this to suggest that something be done for me."}, {"start_ms": 119667, "end_ms": 123607, "text": "Indeed, I would rather die than let anyone nullify my boast."}, {"start_ms": 124447, "end_ms": 130188, "text": "Yet when I preach the gospel, I have no reason to boast, because I am obligated to preach."}, {"start_ms": 130908, "end_ms": 133368, "text": "Woe to me if I do not preach the gospel!"}, {"start_ms": 134048, "end_ms": 136888, "text": "If my preaching is voluntary, I have a reward."}, {"start_ms": 137288, "end_ms": 142209, "text": "But if it is not voluntary, I am still entrusted with a responsibility."}, {"start_ms": 143029, "end_ms": 144529, "text": "What then is my reward?"}, {"start_ms": 145189, "end_ms": 151869, "text": "That in preaching the gospel I may offer it free of charge, and so not use up my rights in preaching it."}, {"start_ms": 153469, "end_ms": 160150, "text": "Though I am free of obligation to anyone, I make myself a slave to everyone, to win as many as possible."}, {"start_ms": 160690, "end_ms": 163750, "text": "To the Jews I became like a Jew, to win the Jews."}, {"start_ms": 164250, "end_ms": 172170, "text": "To those under the law I became like one under the law (though I myself am not under the law), to win those under the law."}, {"start_ms": 172850, "end_ms": 182691, "text": "To those without the law I became like one without the law (though I am not outside the law of God but am under the law of Christ), to win those without the law."}, {"start_ms": 183571, "end_ms": 185951, "text": "To the weak I became weak, to win the weak."}, {"start_ms": 186611, "end_ms": 192132, "text": "I have become all things to all people so that by all possible means I might save some."}, {"start_ms": 193432, "end_ms": 197752, "text": "I do all this for the sake of the gospel, so that I may share in its blessings."}, {"start_ms": 198272, "end_ms": 203832, "text": "Do you not know that in a race all the runners run, but only one receives the prize?"}, {"start_ms": 204492, "end_ms": 207092, "text": "Run in such a way as to take the prize."}, {"start_ms": 207812, "end_ms": 211693, "text": "Everyone who competes in the games trains with strict discipline."}, {"start_ms": 212213, "end_ms": 217753, "text": "They do it for a crown that is perishable, but we do it for a crown that is imperishable."}, {"start_ms": 218373, "end_ms": 223353, "text": "Therefore I do not run aimlessly; I do not fight like I am beating the air."}, {"start_ms": 223933, "end_ms": 232394, "text": "No, I discipline my body and make it my slave, so that after I have preached to others, I myself will not be disqualified."}], "words": [{"t": "1", "s": 0, "e": 2380, "si": 0}, {"t": "Corinthians,", "s": 2380, "e": 3140, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 3140, "e": 3480, "si": 0}, {"t": "Nine.", "s": 3520, "e": 5160, "si": 0}, {"t": "Am", "s": 5160, "e": 5240, "si": 1}, {"t": "I", "s": 5400, "e": 5420, "si": 1}, {"t": "not", "s": 5500, "e": 5700, "si": 1}, {"t": "free?", "s": 5800